 "v1_problem": "Dispute tickets roughly doubled since August 2026 (≈600→1260/month) even though response times stay within SLA and no tariff change occurred, so the surge reflects genuine upstream billing errors rather than response capacity or rate changes. The best-supported mechanism is a change in billing import/validation processing around August: 59% of disputed bills were computed from ACTUAL meter reads (not estimates), so the majority of errors cannot be explained by estimate substitution and instead point to the billing import/validation step itself producing or accepting incorrect bills.",
